    buf = buf + "\n"
    buf = buf + "// ── batch 11 (ING #35 r26) — CARRIER-EMIT: file-static DATA carrier ──\n"
    buf = buf + "//  RFC061 r26 falsifies the r24 census's '(C) forbidden-wall' for the\n"
    buf = buf + "//  _hx_stats counter carrier. The census claimed hexa_array_alloc /\n"
    buf = buf + "//  hexa_array_zeros_float are unportable because their bodies touch the\n"
    buf = buf + "//  file-static counters (_hx_stats_array_new) + guard (_hx_stats_on) that\n"
    buf = buf + "//  live in self/runtime_core.c — which the drop path DROPS from the compile,\n"
    buf = buf + "//  so the seed would see no carrier → 'needs frozen-blob de-static (forbidden)'.\n"
    buf = buf + "//  MEASURED FALSE: the carrier is a *file-static*, so emitting a FRESH copy of\n"
    buf = buf + "//  it co-located with the body IN THIS SEED TU collides with NOTHING — the\n"
    buf = buf + "//  frozen runtime_core.c's static copy is in the DROPPED/uncompiled TU, and a\n"
    buf = buf + "//  file-static exports no link symbol, so there is no duplicate-definition at\n"
    buf = buf + "//  the final link either. The body then resolves _hx_stats_on / _hx_stats_\n"
